meta {
  name: Create Daily Log - Health & Wellbeing
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/young-persons/:youngperson/daily-logs
  body: multipartForm
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  youngperson: 1
  house: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:multipart-form {
  chronology_id: 4
  wellbeing_category: Physical Wellbeing
  action_observation: Young person participated in sports activities. Showed good physical stamina and coordination. No health concerns noted.
  mood[0]: Happy
  mood[1]: Content
  clothing: Tracksuit and running shoes
  breakfast: Porridge with banana
  lunch: Chicken salad sandwich
  dinner: Grilled fish with vegetables
  wake_up_time: 07:00
  wake_up_notes: Woke up refreshed
  ~attachments[0]: @file(/path/to/health_report.pdf)
}

docs {
  # Create Daily Log - Health & Wellbeing
  
  Create a daily log for health and wellbeing activities.
  
  ## Required Fields (Health & Wellbeing)
  - `chronology_id` (integer): Must be 4 (Health & Wellbeing)
  
  **Note:** `date`, `log_date_time`, and `day_part` are automatically set by the server.
  - `wellbeing_category` (string, required): Physical Wellbeing, Emotional wellbeing, Mental wellbeing, Sleep and Rest
  - `action_observation` (string, required): Detailed observation or action taken
  
  ## Optional Fields
  - `day_part` (string): Auto-detected if not provided (Morning/Afternoon/Evening/Night)
  - `mood` (array): Young person's mood
  - `clothing` (string): What the young person is wearing
  - `breakfast`, `lunch`, `dinner`, `snacks` (string): Meal details
  - `wake_up_time` (time): Wake up time (HH:MM)
  - `wake_up_notes` (string): Notes about waking up
  - `attachments` (files): Health reports, photos, etc.
  
  ## Example Wellbeing Categories
  - Physical Wellbeing: Exercise, medical checkups, physical activities
  - Emotional wellbeing: Counseling sessions, emotional support
  - Mental wellbeing: Therapy, mindfulness activities
  - Sleep and Rest: Sleep patterns, rest periods
  
  ## Response (201 Created)
  Returns the created daily log activity with auto-detected day_part based on log_date_time.
}
